# Deploy target (SSH creds/path for deploy.sh) -- never commit
.deploy.env
# Acceptance/stage tests -- the SYNTHETIC harness below drives the live pipeline
# with fake frames, so it is dev tooling rather than a shipped suite and stays
# local. Everything ELSE under tests/ is tracked -- including tests/live/_synth.py,
# which the harness and the plan-item regression tests both import. Leaving
# _synth.py untracked while tracking its importers made `python tests/run_all.py`
# fail on every fresh clone with ModuleNotFoundError; do not un-track it again.
#
# Listed file-by-file rather than as `tests/*` plus negations: plan-item tests now
# live under tests/live/ alongside the harness, and a blanket exclude would need
# `git add -f` for each new one -- a test silently left off the remote is exactly
# the failure this list exists to prevent.
tests/live/run_stage3_acceptance.py
tests/live/test_stage2_parallel_inference.py
tests/live/test_stage3_*.py
tests/live/test_stage6_offline_reconcile.py

# tests/calibration/ IS tracked. Unlike the synthetic stage tests, it measures on
# REAL footage and produces the numbers REMEDIATION_PLAN.md Part H depends on, so
# those scripts are the source of truth for every threshold decision and must not
# live only on one machine. See tests/calibration/README.md.

# Local design/planning notes -- kept out of git by choice. NOTE: because these are
# untracked, git carries no history for them, so any revision record has to live
# inside the documents themselves (see ADR-003 section 7).
NVIDIA_DeepStream_Adoption_Plan.md
ADR-003-geometric-signal.md
ADR-003A-geometry-subsystem.md
ADR-003B-label-mining.md
ADR-003C-identity-integration.md

